*[[2026 Nepal floods]]
**[[Flash flood]]s and [[Mudflow|mudslide]]s along the [[Trishuli River]] impact [[Nepal]] and [[Greater Tibet|Tibet]]. At least 160 people are killed, hundreds are injured and 463 others, including over 200 [[Tourism in Nepal|tourists]], are reported missing in Nepal, while [[Chinese Communist Party]] officials report three deaths and 265 missing in Tibet, severely affecting [[Gyirong County]] and its [[Gyirong Port|port]]. [https://www.jamaicaobserver.com/2026/08/26/massive-flood-near-tibet-border-kills-least-95-nepal/ (AFP via ''Jamaica Observer'')] [https://en.nepalkhabar.com/news/detail/19548/ (Nepalkhabar)] [https://ekantipur.com/politics/2026/08/26/earthquake-caused-avalanches-floods-government-01-44.html (''Kantipur'')] [https://japantoday.com/category/world/hundreds-missing-and-at-least-8-killed-after-avalanche-triggers-deadly-flash-floods-in-nepal (''Japan Today'')]
**[[Government of Nepal|Nepali officials]] say bridges, roads, [[power station]]s, and entire villages have been swept away by the [[flash flood]]ing with some areas still completely cut-off from [[search and rescue]] efforts. [https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/asia/2026/08/26/nepal-tibet-flash-floods/ (''The National'')]
